      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The deputy pulls up a stool at the counter, his eyes locked on Bubba and the others. \"I couldn't help but overhear,\" he says, his voice even and measured. \"I think we need to talk about what's going on here. We can't just let these... outsiders come in and disrupt our way of life.\" He pauses, studying the room before continuing. \"We need to maintain order, keep the peace. And that means making sure certain... elements of our community stay in their place.\" He glances at Bubba, his expression neutral. \"Now, I know some folks might say we're being too strict, too reactionary. But I say, if we don't keep these... influences at bay, they'll be the ones causing the trouble. They'll be the ones breaking the law, disturbing the peace.\" He leans in, his voice taking on a slightly harder edge. \"We can't let that happen. We need to protect our town, our way of life. And that means making some tough decisions.\"",
